          "returnType": "Voice",
          "description": "Implements Playable. Called by AudioSystem.play. Stops any previously active voice (a stream has a single playhead), then starts a fresh AudioStreamVoice. Throws on a destroyed stream. The check is unconditional, not __DEV__-only: createMediaElementSource() may be called exactly once per media element, and the second call raises InvalidStateError in the browser - a hard, hard-to-trace runtime failure that a production build must not walk into."
        },
